.TH SDL_GPUBufferUsageFlags 3type "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 DATATYPES"
.SH NAME
SDL_GPUBufferUsageFlags \- Specifies how a buffer is intended to be used by the client.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_gpu.h>
.PP
.BI "typedef Uint32 SDL_GPUBufferUsageFlags;
.BI "
.BI "#define SDL_GPU_BUFFERUSAGE_VERTEX                                  (1u << 0) /**< Buffer is a vertex buffer. */
.BI "#define SDL_GPU_BUFFERUSAGE_INDEX                                   (1u << 1) /**< Buffer is an index buffer. */
.BI "#define SDL_GPU_BUFFERUSAGE_INDIRECT                                (1u << 2) /**< Buffer is an indirect buffer. */
.BI "#define SDL_GPU_BUFFERUSAGE_GRAPHICS_STORAGE_READ                   (1u << 3) /**< Buffer supports storage reads in graphics stages. */
.BI "#define SDL_GPU_BUFFERUSAGE_COMPUTE_STORAGE_READ                    (1u << 4) /**< Buffer supports storage reads in the compute stage. */
.BI "#define SDL_GPU_BUFFERUSAGE_COMPUTE_STORAGE_WRITE                   (1u << 5) /**< Buffer supports storage writes in the compute stage. */
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
A buffer must have at least one usage flag\[char46]
.PP
If a buffer has multiple read usages, this may lead to a performance penalty due to more conservative memory barriers, but it also may not necessarily affect the performance\[char46]
.PP
Unlike textures, READ | WRITE can be used for simultaneous read-write usage\[char46] The same data synchronization concerns as textures apply\[char46]
.PP
If you use a STORAGE flag, the data in the buffer must respect std430 layout conventions\[char46] In practical terms this means you must ensure that vec3 and vec4 fields are 16-byte aligned\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This datatype is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_CreateGPUBuffer (3)
